        "text": "All the requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory with the necessary AWS integration code. Here are the files:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] upload_object.py** - uploads a file or byte stream to managed object storage using AWS S3.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] presigned_download.py** - creates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object using AWS S3.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] object_metadata.py** - reads object metadata or head information from managed object storage using AWS S3.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] list_prefix.py** - lists stored objects under a bucket or container prefix using AWS S3.\n5. **[HELPER] storage_client.py** - provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Object Storage using AWS S3.\n6. **[HELPER] storage_models.py** - defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Object Storage using AWS S3.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] stored_document_ocr.py** - runs OCR on a stored document object using AWS S3 and Python libraries.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] stored_text_translate.py** - translates text extracted from a stored document using AWS S3 and Python libraries.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] stored_asset_summary.py** - summarizes content extracted from a stored asset using AWS S3 and Python libraries.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] asset_metadata_embedding.py** - embeds object metadata and extracted text for search using AWS S3 and Python libraries.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS and makes the provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files provide configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful. The later-step files use additional AWS services for more advanced tasks like OCR, text translation, summarization, and metadata embedding.",
